# cmd.exe mis-parses a multi-line `if ( ... )` block when the batch file has
# LF-only endings, and the documented Windows install route is "download the
# GitHub zip", which hands the user exactly what is in the tree. Pin these so a
# contributor's core.autocrlf cannot quietly strip the CRs on the way in.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# start.sh runs through a shebang, and a CR at the end of that line becomes
# part of the interpreter path.
*.sh text eol=lf
